# Copy to crawl/.env (gitignored — the repo-root .gitignore ignores every .env), fill in BOTH lines,
# then `docker compose up -d`. Compose reads this for interpolation. Each box (box-c, site-b) has
# its OWN crawl/.env — the same compose, a different env — so nothing about one deployment is in code.
# Both variables use ${VAR:?} in the compose: a missing one fails the boot loudly, never a default.
#
# The host-side (loopback) port the Crawl4AI API is published on. The container always listens on
# 11235; this is only where it appears on 127.0.0.1 of THIS host. Pick a free port that does not
# collide with the other services on the same box (box-c: lb 8010, power 8016).
CRAWL_PORT=11235
#
# The API token. Crawl4AI 0.9.x refuses to serve on a reachable interface without one (it would bind
# the container's own loopback and reset every published-port connection). With a token set it binds
# all interfaces inside the container — still loopback-only on this host via CRAWL_PORT above — and
# requires `Authorization: Bearer <this value>` on every endpoint except GET /health. It is a SECRET:
# generate a fresh one per box and keep it out of git.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
CRAWL_API_TOKEN=replace-with-openssl-rand-hex-32
